WEBVTT

00:00:11.949 --> 00:00:12.759
The new dunning model:

00:00:13.229 --> 00:00:14.039
the results so far.

00:00:16.021 --> 00:00:17.642
A subscription rebill is declined.

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:19.519
Until the third of November,

00:00:19.946 --> 00:00:21.183
in the United States and Canada,

00:00:21.525 --> 00:00:23.957
it got one retry, twelve hours later.

00:00:24.554 --> 00:00:26.303
About eight in every hundred of those

00:00:26.389 --> 00:00:27.199
retries were paid.

00:00:30.425 --> 00:00:31.833
The new model starts with the reason.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.137
When the bank says not now,

00:00:34.521 --> 00:00:35.673
like insufficient funds,

00:00:36.185 --> 00:00:37.721
the rebill goes on the retry list.

00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:39.854
When the card is expired or closed,

00:00:40.238 --> 00:00:40.963
it needs a new card.

00:00:41.337 --> 00:00:42.958
When the bank or the cardholder says

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.110
never, it stops.

00:00:44.835 --> 00:00:46.073
And when the error is our own,

00:00:46.499 --> 00:00:48.163
it gets fixed, not retried.

00:00:51.685 --> 00:00:53.178
Then it gives the rebill time.

00:00:53.818 --> 00:00:55.439
Retry one comes on day four,

00:00:55.951 --> 00:00:57.658
seventy-two hours after the decline,

00:00:58.085 --> 00:00:59.109
since the fourth of November.

00:00:59.582 --> 00:01:01.161
If the bank says not now again,

00:01:01.545 --> 00:01:03.507
retry two comes on day eight,

00:01:03.849 --> 00:01:06.153
ninety-six hours later, since the twenty-third.

00:01:06.579 --> 00:01:08.926
And nothing is charged after day fourteen.

00:01:12.445 --> 00:01:13.145
So how is it doing?

00:01:13.682 --> 00:01:15.772
Take the rebills first declined on the

00:01:15.815 --> 00:01:16.839
same days of the month.

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:20.167
In October, the twelve-hour retry was paid

00:01:20.253 --> 00:01:21.490
about eight times in a hundred.

00:01:22.083 --> 00:01:24.558
In November, the day-four retry was paid

00:01:24.643 --> 00:01:26.222
nearly twelve times in a hundred:

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:28.483
four hundred and twenty-eight retries

00:01:28.611 --> 00:01:30.446
paid, against two hundred and fifty-eight.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:33.513
Both markets gained.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.073
The United States went from about eight in

00:01:36.116 --> 00:01:37.481
a hundred to nearly eleven.

00:01:38.036 --> 00:01:39.827
Canada went from about seven in a hundred

00:01:40.126 --> 00:01:40.826
to eighteen.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.909
That is the whole new model together:

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:45.767
the longer wait, and a wider list of

00:01:45.853 --> 00:01:46.792
not-now answers.

00:01:50.272 --> 00:01:52.021
Day eight has not charged anyone yet.

00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:54.240
Three hundred and eighty-four rebills,

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:55.819
declined again on day four,

00:01:56.203 --> 00:01:57.056
are waiting for it.

00:01:57.653 --> 00:01:59.275
The first are due on the twenty-eighth of

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:00.811
November, and from then on,

00:02:01.195 --> 00:02:02.560
day eight is counted separately.

00:02:04.911 --> 00:02:05.722
The new dunning model:

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:07.898
read the reason, give it time,

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:09.237
try twice.

